# NVIDIA GPU Support — Headless/Compute Only (no X11/GLX)
#
# Driver branch is sourced from NVIDIA's official CUDA repo (see
# config/archives/nvidia-cuda.*) and pinned to 570.133.20-1, the last 570.x
# build whose nvidia-kernel-dkms is satisfied by Debian bookworm's dkms 3.0.10.
# Driver 570 is required: Debian's 535.x cannot load Ollama 0.30.x's CUDA 12.8
# kernel images and fails with "CUDA error: device kernel image is invalid".
#
# nvidia-driver-cuda is NVIDIA's headless CUDA-only package — explicitly
# "does not require a display or graphical output". It bundles nvidia-smi
# (Debian's split nvidia-smi/nvidia-driver-bin packages don't exist upstream).
# nvidia-cuda-toolkit is NOT needed — Ollama bundles its own CUDA runtime.
dkms
linux-headers-amd64
nvidia-kernel-dkms
nvidia-driver-cuda
nvidia-persistenced
firmware-nvidia-gsp
libcuda1
libnvidia-ml1
nvidia-modprobe
